## Summary

**Phase 2 Tools**:
1. ✅ `decide_chunking_strategy` - Determines chunking approach (should_chunk=true for 24 pages >= 10 threshold)
2. ✅ `chunk_markdown` - Creates chunks (5 chunks by H1 headings when strategy="by_h1")
3. ✅ `build_index` - Builds section index from chunks (5 sections, one per chunk/H1 heading)
4. ✅ `load_outline_template` - Loads template (optional, may be skipped)

**Key Metrics**:
- Chunking decision: should_chunk=true (24 pages >= 10 page threshold)
- Strategy: "by_h1" (derived from context_aware_level="h1")
- Context aware level: "h1" (user chosen)
- Chunks created: 5 (one per H1 heading)
- Sections in index: 5 (one per chunk, mapped 1:1)
- All sections status: "unmapped" (will be mapped in Phase 3)
- Template: Optional (may be skipped if not configured)

**Important Notes**:
- With threshold=10 pages and document having 24 pages, chunking is now **enabled** (was disabled with threshold=50)
- With context_aware_level="h1", the document is chunked by H1 headings (5 chunks)
- Each chunk contains all content from one H1 heading to the next (including all nested H2 headings and content)
- The index has 5 sections (one per chunk/H1 heading), not 57 sections (which would be H2 level)
- This is a coarser-grained chunking strategy compared to H2 chunking
